From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:33:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] arm: mediatek: add MT8127 support

U-Boot runs on the MT8127 as a second stage after the vendor LK
bootloader, which has already set up DRAM, clocks and the PMIC wrapper:
no SPL and no low-level init.

The vendor boot chain leaves GPT6 off, which gates the clock of the
generic timer counter, and does not program CNTFRQ: enable GPT6 like
Linux does and set the 13 MHz counter rate at build time.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig         | 11 +++++
 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Makefile        |  1 +
 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8127/Makefile |  3 ++
 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8127/init.c   | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/configs/mt8127.h               | 19 +++++++++
 5 files changed, 92 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8127/Makefile
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8127/init.c
 create mode 100644 include/configs/mt8127.h

